ore access control mechanism.\n\n**Answer: (B) High**", "thinking": "Let me analyze the function \"common_perm_cond\" based on the provided domain knowledge.\n\nFunction name: common_perm_cond\nFunction description: \"common perm cond common permission wrapper around inode cond\"\n\nBreaking this down:\n- \"perm\" is a common abbreviation for \"permission\"\n- The description explicitly mentions \"common permission wrapper\"\n- This is clearly related to permission checking/wrapping functionality\n\nLooking at the classification criteria:\n\n**Class 0 (Not High)**: General system utilities, hardware/driver interactions, basic resource management (read, write, map, unregister, validate, check, basic get/set operations). No access control or privilege management logic.\n\n**Class 1 (High)**: Security enforcement, access control management, capability checks, system-wide privileged configurations. Keywords include \"privilege\", \"capable\", \"security\", \"permission\", \"acl\", \"sid\", \"policy\", \"relabel\", and security module names. Logic patterns center around authorizing, altering, or bypassing system-level access controls.\n\nThe function name contains \"perm\" which relates to \"permission\" - this is explicitly listed as a keyword for Class 1 (High). The description also explicitly mentions \"permission wrapper\" which indicates this function is involved in access control/permission checking.\n\nThis function appears to be a common permission checking wrapper for inode conditions, which is clearly related to security enforcement and access control management.\n\nTherefore, this should be classified as Class 1 (High)."}, "done": true, "done_reason": "stop", "total_duration": 17998803782, "prompt_eval_count": 374, "eval_count": 568}}, {"id": "keyctl_get_security", "ground_truth": "1", "prompt": {"model": "glm-5.1:cloud", "messages": [{"role": "system", "content": "You are Frederick, an elite AI cybersecurity expert specializing in vulnerability severity evalu